# ── Your raw broker exports never get committed ─────────────────────
# Real exports carry account numbers and your actual sleeve size. Publish via
#   python3 tools/anonymise.py ~/Downloads/export.csv
# which scales everything to a nominal NAV and writes a *.public.csv — the form
# the negation line below deliberately allows through.
# (gitignore has no inline comments: a trailing "# ..." becomes part of the
#  pattern and silently breaks it. Keep every comment on its own line.)
input/*.csv
input/watchlist.md
input/watchlist_*.md
# your real positions, scaled by tools/anonymise.py — allowed through:
!input/*.public.csv
# the bundled demo book, used only when no real export is present — allowed through:
!input/*.example.csv

# ── Local source config stays local ─────────────────────────────────
# The repo ships input/config/fundamentals.json.example with the publish-safe
# "none" adapter. Your live adapter choice (e.g. "curated") is a local override
# and never commits — otherwise every commit flips the public default.
input/config/fundamentals.json

# Your tracking files are yours; the shipped versions are references.
# Uncomment this line to keep the reference files private:
# input/tracking/*.md

# ── Generated output IS committed, on purpose ───────────────────────
# This repo publishes its own running history — radar reports, evaluations, P&L and
# the gate ledger — so a reader can audit whether the gates actually filtered out
# winners or saved money, rather than taking the rules on trust. That claim is the
# whole point of the ledger and it cannot be checked against an empty folder.
#
# ⚠️  Everything under output/ is therefore PUBLIC. Regenerate it from the scaled
# holdings, never from a real export, or the reports carry the real numbers straight
# past the input/ gitignore above. `python3 tools/checks.py --publish` greps the
# tree for real-NAV strings before any push.
output/.state/
output/ledger/pending_*.csv

# ── Standard ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/agents/.probe
node_modules/
package-lock.json
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.bak
*.bak.*
.venv/
venv/
.env
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
_to_delete/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private providers and the data they read (19 Aug 2026).
#
# These two lines ARE the public/private boundary. `tools/publish.py` builds the
# public tree by declining to copy these directories, and `checks.py --publish`
# FAILs if a provider declaring `private: True` is discoverable in the tree
# being published. Structural, not a text sweep — a grep for vendor names passes
# the moment someone writes "the paid provider" in a docstring.
providers/private/
input/capture/

# Live provider selection. The committed .example ships every leg on `none`, so
# a clone runs honestly; your actual choices never commit.
input/config/providers.json

# tools/rerun.py sandboxes (same-day test re-runs; contain real NAV)
.rerun/
